<p style="margin-top: 24px;"><strong>BE IT ENACTED</strong> as a by-law of the Corporation as follows:</p>

<div class="article-title">I. Interpretation</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.1</span> "Act" means the statute pursuant to which the Corporation is incorporated, including any successor or replacement legislation, together with the regulations made thereunder, in each case as amended from time to time.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.2</span> "Articles" means the articles of incorporation of the Corporation, as amended or restated from time to time.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.3</span> "Board" means the board of directors of the Corporation.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.4</span> "By-Laws" means this by-law and all other by-laws of the Corporation from time to time in force and effect.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.5</span> "Resident Canadian" has the meaning given to it in the Act.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.6</span> "Signing Officer" means, in relation to any instrument, any person authorized to sign the same on behalf of the Corporation by virtue of Article III or by a resolution passed pursuant thereto.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">1.7</span> Words importing the singular include the plural and vice versa; the masculine includes the feminine; and "person" includes an individual, partnership, association, body corporate, trustee, executor, administrator and legal representative.</div>

<div class="article-title">II. Borrowing, Banking and Securities</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">2.1</span> The Corporation has the borrowing powers set out in the Articles and, if not so set out, the directors may, without authorization of the shareholders: (i) borrow money on the credit of the Corporation; (ii) issue, reissue, sell or pledge debt obligations of the Corporation; (iii) subject to the Act, give a guarantee on behalf of the Corporation to secure performance of an obligation of any person; and (iv) mortgage, hypothecate, pledge or otherwise create a security interest in all or any property of the Corporation, owned or subsequently acquired, to secure any obligation of the Corporation.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">3.1</span> The Board may from time to time delegate any of the powers of the directors to a committee of the Board or to a managing director, subject to the provisions of the Act.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">4.1</span> The banking business of the Corporation, including the borrowing of money and the giving of security therefor, will be transacted with such banks, trust companies or other financial institutions as may from time to time be designated by or under the authority of the Board, on such terms as the Board may prescribe.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">5.1</span> All shares and securities owned by the Corporation will be lodged in the name of the Corporation with a chartered bank, a trust company, in a safety deposit box or with such other depository as the Board may from time to time determine.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">6.1</span> The voting rights attached to shares or securities owned by the Corporation may be voted in such manner and by such person as the Board may from time to time determine.</div>

<div class="article-title">III. Execution of Instruments</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">7.1</span> Deeds, transfers, assignments, contracts, obligations and other instruments in writing requiring execution by the Corporation may be signed by any one or more persons designated by the Board, and any such Signing Officer may affix the corporate seal (if any) thereto. The Board may from time to time direct the manner in which, and the person(s) by whom, any particular instrument or class of instruments may or shall be signed.</div>

<div class="article-title">IV. Directors</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">8.1</span> The affairs and business of the Corporation will be managed or supervised by its Board.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">9.1</span> Subject to the Articles or a Unanimous Shareholders Agreement, the number of directors will be that determined by the shareholders from time to time, of whom at least the proportion required by the Act will be Resident Canadians.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">10.1</span> The election of directors takes place at each annual meeting of shareholders. Retiring directors are eligible for re-election. If an election of directors is not held at the proper time, the incumbent directors continue in office until their successors are elected.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">11.1</span> Subject to the Act, the shareholders may by ordinary resolution passed at a meeting specially called for such purpose remove any director from office, except a director elected by a class or series with a separate right of election. The vacancy created by such removal may be filled at the same meeting; failing which it may be filled by the Board.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">12.1</span> No person is qualified for election as a director if he or she is less than 18 years of age, has been found by a court to be of unsound mind, is not an individual, or has the status of a bankrupt. A director need not be a shareholder.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">13.1</span> No election or appointment of a person as a director is effective unless that person was present at the meeting and did not refuse to act, or consents in writing to act before or within ten (10) days after the election or appointment, or thereafter acts as a director pursuant to such election or appointment.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">14.1</span> A director ceases to hold office upon death, removal, ceasing to be qualified, or upon delivery of a written resignation to the Corporation. As long as a quorum of directors remains in office, vacancies on the Board may be filled by the remaining directors. Where there is no quorum, the directors then in office shall forthwith call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancies.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">15.1</span> The directors may appoint from among their number one or more committees of the Board, and subject to the Act may delegate to any such committee any of the powers of the directors. At least the proportion of Resident Canadians required by the Act will be members of any such committee.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">16.1</span> Subject to any Unanimous Shareholders Agreement, the directors will be paid such reasonable remuneration for their services as the Board may from time to time determine, and will be entitled to be reimbursed for travelling and other expenses properly incurred in attending meetings of the Board or otherwise discharging their duties.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">17.1</span> Whenever the Corporation has only one director, every provision of these By-Laws inconsistent with the existence of only one director is deemed amended so as to remove such inconsistency. The sole director possesses all powers and authority that would otherwise be vested in the Board, no notice of meetings is required, no quorum is required, and a written declaration by the sole director is as valid as if passed at a duly constituted meeting.</div>

<div class="article-title">V. Meetings of Directors</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">18.1</span> Meetings of the Board and of committees may be held within or outside the jurisdiction of incorporation. Notice of the time and place of each meeting will be given to each director not less than 48 hours before the time of the meeting; no notice need specify the purpose of the meeting. A director may waive notice in any manner, and attendance at a meeting constitutes waiver, except where the director attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of business on the grounds that the meeting was not lawfully called.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">19.1</span> A majority of the directors in office constitutes a quorum, and notwithstanding vacancies the remaining directors may exercise all the powers of the Board so long as a quorum remains. The Board will not transact business at a meeting (other than filling a vacancy on the Board) unless at least the proportion of Resident Canadians required by the Act is present, except where a Resident Canadian director who is unable to be present approves the business in writing or by electronic means.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">20.1</span> Each director present has one vote. Questions are decided by a majority of votes; in the case of a tie, the chair of the meeting does not have a casting vote. A director may participate in a meeting by means of telephone or other communication facility that permits all persons participating to communicate adequately, and is deemed present at the meeting.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">21.1</span> A resolution in writing signed by all the directors entitled to vote on that resolution at a meeting of the Board (or a committee) is as valid as if it had been passed at a meeting duly called and held.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">22.1</span> A director who is present at a meeting is deemed to have consented to any resolution passed or action taken thereat unless the director: (a) requests that his or her dissent be entered in the minutes; (b) sends a written dissent to the secretary before the meeting is adjourned; (c) sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office immediately after the meeting is adjourned; or (d) otherwise proves that he or she did not consent to the resolution or action. A director who votes for or consents to a resolution is not entitled to dissent.</div>

<div class="article-title">VI. Protection of Directors, Officers and Others</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">23.1</span> A director or officer is not disqualified, nor required to vacate office, by reason only that he or she is a party to or has a material interest in any person who is a party to a material contract or proposed material contract with the Corporation, provided the director or officer discloses the nature and extent of that interest as required by the Act and the contract is approved by the Board or shareholders and is reasonable and fair to the Corporation when so approved.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">24.1</span> Every director and officer in exercising powers and discharging duties will act honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the Corporation, and will exercise the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances. Subject to the foregoing, no director or officer is liable for the acts, receipts, neglects or defaults of any other director, officer or employee, for joining in any receipt or act for conformity, or for any loss, damage or expense happening to the Corporation through the insufficiency of title to property acquired or of any security upon which monies of the Corporation are placed, except as the Act provides.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">25.1</span> Subject to the Act, the Corporation will indemnify a director or officer, a former director or officer, or a person who acts or acted at the Corporation's request as a director or officer of another body corporate, and his or her heirs and legal representatives, against any liability and all costs, charges and expenses reasonably incurred in respect of any civil, criminal, administrative, investigative or other proceeding to which he or she is involved by reason of being or having been a director or officer, except where such liability relates to the failure to act honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the Corporation.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">26.1</span> The Corporation may purchase and maintain insurance for the benefit of any person referred to in section 25.1 against any liability incurred by such person in his or her capacity as a director or officer.</div>

<div class="article-title">VII. Officers</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">27.1</span> The Board from time to time will elect or appoint a President and a Secretary, and may elect or appoint a Chairman of the Board, a Managing Director, one or more Vice-Presidents, a Treasurer and such other officers as the Board may determine, including one or more assistants. One person may hold more than one office.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">28.1</span> The Chairman of the Board, if any, must be a director and (where required by the Act) a Resident Canadian, and will when present preside at all meetings of the Board, of committees, and (in the absence of the President) of shareholders.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">29.1</span> The Managing Director, if any, will exercise such powers and have such authority as the Board may delegate, in accordance with the Act.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">30.1</span> The President is the Chief Executive Officer of the Corporation and, subject to the authority of the Board and any Managing Director, has such other powers and duties as the Board may specify.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">31.1</span> A Vice-President will, during the absence or disability of the President, perform the duties and exercise the powers of the President (provided that a Vice-President who is not a director will not preside at any meeting of the Board), and will have such other powers and duties as the Board or the President may prescribe.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">32.1</span> The Secretary will attend all meetings of the Board, shareholders and committees, will keep the minutes thereof, will give all notices required, will be the custodian of the corporate seal (if any) and of all books, papers, records, documents and instruments belonging to the Corporation, and will have such other powers and duties as the Board or the Chief Executive Officer may specify.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">33.1</span> The Treasurer will keep proper accounting records in compliance with the Act, will be responsible for the deposit of money, the safekeeping of securities and the disbursement of funds, and will render to the Board whenever required an account of all the Treasurer's transactions.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">34.1</span> The General Manager, if appointed, will have, subject to the authority of the Board, the Managing Director and the President, full power to manage and direct the business and affairs of the Corporation (except such matters as by law must be transacted by the Board or shareholders) and to employ and discharge agents and employees of the Corporation.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">35.1</span> The powers and duties of all other officers will be such as the terms of their engagement call for or as the Board, the Managing Director or the President may specify. The Board may from time to time vary, add to or limit the powers and duties of any officer; fill any office that becomes vacant; determine the remuneration of officers; and remove any officer with or without cause.</div>

<div class="article-title">VIII. Shareholders' Meetings</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">36.1</span> The Board will call an annual meeting of shareholders not later than 15 months after the last preceding annual meeting and within the period required by the Act, and may at any time call a special meeting of shareholders.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">37.1</span> Meetings of shareholders will be held at the registered office of the Corporation or at such other place as the Board may determine. The Board may fix in advance a record date, preceding any meeting of shareholders by not more than 50 nor less than 21 days, for determination of the shareholders entitled to notice of the meeting. Notice of the time and place of each meeting will be given not less than 21 nor more than 50 days before the meeting.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">38.1</span> A quorum at any meeting of shareholders is one or more persons present in person or represented by proxy holding or representing not less than a majority of the outstanding shares entitled to vote. Each shareholder is entitled to one vote per voting share. Notice may be waived in any manner, and attendance constitutes waiver, except where the person attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of business on the grounds that the meeting was not lawfully called.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">39.1</span> If all the shareholders entitled to vote consent, a shareholder may participate in a meeting by means of telephone or other communication facility that permits all persons participating to communicate adequately, and is deemed present at the meeting.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">40.1</span> Votes at meetings of shareholders may be cast either personally or by proxy. A proxy will be executed by the shareholder or his or her duly authorized attorney, and is valid only at the meeting in respect of which it is given or any adjournment thereof. A proxy holder need not be a shareholder. A proxy may be in substantially the following form: <em>"The undersigned shareholder of [Corporation] hereby appoints [Name] of [Address], or failing him/her [Alternate], as the nominee of the undersigned to attend and act for the undersigned and on behalf of the undersigned at the [type of meeting] meeting of the shareholders of the Corporation to be held on the [date] and at any adjournment thereof. Dated [date]. ____________________ Signature of Shareholder."</em> The Board may specify in the notice of meeting a time, not more than 48 hours (excluding Saturdays and holidays) before the meeting, by which proxies must be deposited.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">41.1</span> Subject to the Act, any question at a meeting of shareholders will be decided by a show of hands unless a ballot is required or demanded. A shareholder, proxyholder or other person entitled to vote may demand and the chairman will require that a ballot be taken either before or upon the declaration of the result of any vote by show of hands. On a ballot each person present has, in respect of the shares he or she is entitled to vote, the number of votes provided by the Articles or, in the absence of such provision, one vote per share. Questions are decided by a majority of votes cast; in case of an equality of votes the matter is lost.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">42.1</span> Where two or more persons hold shares jointly, any one of them present in person or duly represented may, in the absence of the other(s), vote the shares; but if two or more of such persons are present and vote, they shall vote as one the shares jointly held.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">43.1</span> The chairman of a meeting of shareholders may, with the consent of the meeting, adjourn the meeting from time to time and from place to place. If the meeting is adjourned for less than 30 days, no notice of the adjourned meeting other than announcement at the time of adjournment is required.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">44.1</span> A resolution in writing signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on that resolution at a meeting of shareholders is as valid as if it had been passed at a meeting of the shareholders. Where the Corporation has only one shareholder, that shareholder present in person or duly represented constitutes a meeting.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">45.1</span> Resolutions and minutes of meetings requiring signature of those attending may be signed in counterpart, and signatures delivered by electronic means are deemed to be original signatures.</div>

<div class="article-title">IX. Shares</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">46.1</span> Subject to the Act, the Articles, the rights of the holders of any class of shares and any Unanimous Shareholders Agreement, the Board may from time to time issue shares of the Corporation to such persons and for such consideration as the Board may determine, provided no share is issued until fully paid in money, in property or in past services.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">47.1</span> The Board may from time to time authorize the Corporation to pay a reasonable commission to any person in consideration of that person purchasing or agreeing to purchase shares of the Corporation, or procuring or agreeing to procure purchasers for any such shares.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">48.1</span> Subject to the Act, the Corporation will treat the registered holder of any share as the person exclusively entitled to vote, to receive notices, to receive any dividend or other payments in respect of the share, and otherwise to exercise all the rights and powers of an owner of the share.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">49.1</span> Every shareholder is entitled, without payment, to a share certificate in respect of the shares held by them as shown by the records of the Corporation, in such form as the Board may approve and signed in accordance with the Act. Where two or more persons are registered as joint holders of any share, the Corporation is not bound to issue more than one certificate, and delivery to one of the joint holders is sufficient delivery to all.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">50.1</span> The Board (or any officer or agent designated by the Board) may direct the issue of a new share certificate in lieu of and upon cancellation of a certificate that has been mutilated, or in substitution for a certificate claimed to have been lost, destroyed or wrongfully taken, on payment of such reasonable fee and on such terms as to indemnity and evidence of loss and of title as the Board may from time to time prescribe.</div>

<div class="article-title">X. Transfer of Securities</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">51.1</span> The transfer of shares in the Corporation is restricted in accordance with the method set out in the Articles and, where applicable, in any Unanimous Shareholders Agreement.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">52.1</span> A central securities register of the Corporation will be kept at the registered office (or at such other office of the Corporation, or at the office of an agent, as the Board may designate). The register will contain particulars of every issuance and transfer of shares, including the name and latest known address of each holder, the number of shares held, and the date and particulars of each issue, transfer and cancellation.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">53.1</span> In the event of the death of a holder, or of one of the joint holders, of any share, the Corporation will not be required to make any entry in the securities register in respect thereof or to make any dividend or other payment in respect thereof except upon production of all such documents as may be required by law and upon compliance with the reasonable requirements of the Corporation.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">54.1</span> If the Articles so provide, the Corporation has a lien on shares registered in the name of a shareholder for any debt of that shareholder to the Corporation, and may enforce such lien by sale of the shares or by any other action authorized at law or in equity. Pending such enforcement, the Corporation may refuse to register a transfer of the whole or any part of such shares.</div>

<div class="article-title">XI. Dividends and Rights</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">55.1</span> Subject to the Act and the Articles, the Board may from time to time declare and the Corporation may pay dividends to the shareholders according to their respective rights and interests in the Corporation. The Board may fix in advance a record date for the determination of persons entitled to receive payment of a dividend.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">56.1</span> A dividend payable in money will be paid by cheque to the order of each registered holder of shares of the class or series in respect of which it has been declared, and mailed to such registered holder at the address recorded in the Corporation's securities register. The mailing of such cheque, unless not paid on due presentation, satisfies and discharges the liability for the dividend. In the event of non-receipt of any dividend cheque, the Corporation will issue a replacement cheque on such terms as to indemnity, reimbursement of expenses and evidence of non-receipt and of title as the Board may from time to time prescribe.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">57.1</span> Any dividend unclaimed after a period of six (6) years from the date on which the same has been declared to be payable will be forfeited and revert to the Corporation.</div>

<div class="article-title">XII. Information Available to Shareholders</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">58.1</span> Except as provided by the Act, no shareholder is entitled to obtain information respecting any details or conduct of the Corporation's business which, in the opinion of the directors, it would be inappropriate in the interests of the Corporation to communicate to the shareholder.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">59.1</span> The directors may from time to time, subject to rights conferred by the Act, determine whether and to what extent and at what time and place and under what conditions the documents, books, registers and accounting records of the Corporation will be open to the inspection of shareholders.</div>

<div class="article-title">XIII. Notices</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">60.1</span> Any notice required to be given to a shareholder, director, officer or auditor may be delivered personally, sent by prepaid mail, or sent by electronic means in accordance with the Act, addressed to the recipient at the latest address shown in the records of the Corporation. A notice will be deemed to have been given when delivered personally; three business days after deposit in a post office or public letter box if mailed; or 24 hours after dispatch if sent by electronic means.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">61.1</span> If two or more persons are registered as joint holders of any share, any notice may be addressed to all of such joint holders, but notice addressed to one of such persons is sufficient notice to all of them. Every person who, by operation of law, transfer, death of a shareholder or otherwise, becomes entitled to any share is bound by every notice in respect of such share given to the shareholder from whom title is derived prior to the new holder's name being entered on the securities register.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">62.1</span> If a notice or document sent to a shareholder by prepaid mail is returned on three consecutive occasions, no further notice or document need be sent until the shareholder informs the Corporation in writing of a new address. The accidental omission to give any notice, or the non-receipt of any notice, or any error in any notice not affecting the substance thereof, will not invalidate any action taken at any meeting held pursuant to such notice or otherwise founded thereon.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">63.1</span> The signature of any director or officer to any notice or document to be given by the Corporation may be written, stamped, typewritten, printed or applied by electronic means. Any person entitled to notice may at any time waive notice (or abridge the time for notice), whether before or after the meeting or other event, and such waiver or abridgement cures any default in giving or in the time of such notice.</div>

<div class="article-title">XIV. Miscellaneous</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">64.1</span> The financial year of the Corporation will end on <%= company.fiscalYearEnd || 'December 31' %> in each year, or on such other date as the Board may from time to time determine.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">65.1</span> The directors will not, without the prior approval of the shareholders entitled to vote at an annual meeting of the Corporation, given by ordinary resolution, amend or repeal any provision of this by-law.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">66.1</span> This by-law comes into force on the day it is enacted by the Board.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">67.1</span> To the extent that there is any conflict between this by-law and any mandatory provision of the Act, the Act will prevail.</div>
<div class="clause"><span class="clause-no">68.1</span> The provisions of the by-laws of the Corporation are subject to the provisions of any valid Unanimous Shareholders Agreement with respect to those matters dealt with in the Unanimous Shareholders Agreement that are authorized by the Act.</div>
